From c28f39c9394e1d28969335250230cb761f6d801a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:31:02 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 20/26] ling: MLA prompt attention in the expanded form behind
 TF_LING_PROMPT_MLA=expand (default absorbed): kv_b over 2,048-key blocks of
 cache rows on the lane, tf_ling_pattn flash tiles at 192 q.k / 128 v dims
 with an fp32 carry across blocks (ling_glue image; GLM's glue untouched); a
 split cache gathers each 1,024 positions' two pages through b.lat; scratch
 inside the unused absorbed areas (no new memory); decode stays absorbed.
 Kernel contract: tf_ling_pattn gates 1-4 (ling-contract 27/27), gate-5
 records nvcc 13.0/13.3. TP=1 trial pack 16K: expand vs absorbed rel L2
 7.6e-4, greedy 9/9; cut at 9,000 byte-equal to uncut; resumed == fresh 9/9;
 real layer 7 vs exllamav3 4.09e-2 (absorbed 4.05e-2). ling-tp:
 TF_LING_TP_CHUNKS=1 times each chunk

